course: dictionary
lesson: 3357
title: Exceptions to the rule
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An exception is a thing or person that does not follow the usual rule or pattern. Most plurals add an s, but «children» is an exception to that rule. Spot the rule first, then look for the words that break it.
explain: Spelling has many exceptions. «I before e, except after c» is a helpful rule, but words like «weird» and «science» break it. A rule works for most words, and a short list of exceptions is learned on its own.
explain: To make an exception is to allow something that is not usually allowed. In «all numbers except 7», the number 7 is left out. In everyday life, a parent may «make an exception» for a birthday and let you stay up late. Phrases like «with the exception of» and «without exception» help you say exactly which things are included or left out.
fact: An exception is something that does not follow the usual rule.
fact: «Make an exception» means to allow something that is not usually allowed.
fact: «With the exception of» means leaving something out, as in «all numbers except 7».
fact: «Without exception» means every single one, with none left out.
fact: «L'été» (summer) and «le côté» (the side) are masculine exceptions, because most -té words in French are feminine.
exercise: «I before e, except after c» has many exceptions. What is an exception? | A very long word | A rule that always works | *A thing that does not follow the usual rule | A spelling mistake made on purpose
exercise: «All numbers except 7» means that which number is left out? | Every number | *7 | 17 | 8
exercise: Mum says, «I will make an exception for your birthday.» What does make an exception mean? | *Allow something that is not usually allowed | Forget the rule completely | Argue with a rule until it changes | Stop something that was allowed
test: «Liberté, égalité, fraternité are all feminine, like most -té words; l'été is a masculine exception.» Why is l'été in this sentence? | Because it is the same as the other words | Because it is the longest word | *Because it breaks the usual pattern | Because it is a number
test: What does «with the exception of» mean? | Doing something without any rules | Adding something extra | *Leaving something out | Being offended by something
exam: What does «without exception» mean? | *Every one, with none left out | Not allowed at all | Only one thing, and no others | Taken as a rule for a short time
